- kAssigned → dispatch
- kDeferred → mission stays queued (keep_queued)
- kIndeterminate → pause auto assignment
- kRejected → fail mission

And the scan loop semantics: deferred/indeterminate → continue scanning next candidate; rejected → cancel + fail. Also the "saw_indeterminate"/"saw_deferred" aggregation at the end: if ready empty and saw_indeterminate → pause auto assignment; else if saw_deferred → keep queued & re-arm.

Let me design the header `dispatch_assignment_decision.hpp`:

```cpp
namespace amr_dispatcher_ros {

enum class AssignmentDisposition {
  kDispatch,      // 选到车，继续派发
  kKeepQueued,    // 暂时不可用 -> 任务留队，下 tick 重试
  kPauseAutoAssignment,  // 状态不确定 -> 暂停自动分配
  kReject,        // 永久不满足 -> 该单判负
};

struct AssignmentDispositionInput {
  fleet::AssignmentOutcome outcome;
  bool has_any_managed_vehicle = true;  // legacy 单车模式不走选车
};

inline AssignmentDisposition DispositionForOutcome(fleet::AssignmentOutcome outcome);
inline AssignmentDisposition DispositionForOutcome(...);
```

Plus a scan-level aggregation helper:
```cpp
struct DispatchScanSummary {
  bool dispatched = false;
  bool keep_queued = false;
  bool pause_auto_assignment = false;
  bool rejected_any = false;
  bool rearm_queue_start_request = false;  // 留队/暂停时重新武装启动请求
};
```

Hmm, but I want to avoid over-engineering. The dispatcher_node already implements this inline. The cleanest approach that genuinely adds test value: extract the per-candidate disposition AND the scan-summary aggregation into a header-only helper, and have dispatcher_node use it. Then unit test it.

That's a real refactor of dispatcher_node.cpp — risk of breaking. But it's contained: the loop body switch becomes a call.

Actually let me keep it lower risk: create header `dispatch_assignment_decision.hpp` in amr_dispatcher_ros with pure functions, add tests, AND wire dispatcher_node to use it (minimal edits). The semantics must match exactly.

Let me look at the exact loop code again to define the helper precisely.

From the code:
```cpp
for (const auto& candidate_mission : candidates) {
  decision = ... 
  if (kDeferred) { saw_deferred = true; deferred_reason = ...; continue; }
  if (kIndeterminate) { saw_indeterminate = true; indeterminate_reason = ...; continue; }
  if (kRejected) { warn; queue_->Cancel(id); RejectedQueuedMission(...); continue; }
  ... reserve locks ...
}
if (ready.empty()) {
  if (saw_indeterminate) { pause; ReArmQueueStartRequest(); }
  else if (saw_deferred) { warn; ReArmQueueStartRequest(); }
  return;
}
